{"name":"Primal Green","hex":"#11875d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"primal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Being the first in time or in history.","Of greatest importance; primary."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A primal cut (of meat).","The first element of something, especially the first letter of a word."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/primal"},{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"}],"entries":[{"title":"Primal (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Primal is a 2003 action-adventure game developed by Sony Computer Entertainment Europe and published by Sony Computer Entertainment for the PlayStation 2."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c2/Primal_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Primal_(video_game)"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bc/PrimalUnderwaterCombat.jpg/330px-PrimalUnderwaterCombat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/b/bc/PrimalUnderwaterCombat.jpg/330px-PrimalUnderwaterCombat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jen (left) fighting underwater in her Undine form. Her demonic transformations give her access to various new abilities, in this case, to swim, breathe underwater, and use electric energy tentacles to attack.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APrimalUnderwaterCombat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a2/S514_Buffy.png/250px-S514_Buffy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a2/S514_Buffy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/a/a2/S514_Buffy.png/250px-S514_Buffy.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Buffy the Vampire Slayer and its protagonist Buffy Summers (pictured) served as major inspirations for the game and its main character, Jen.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AS514_Buffy.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/2b/Primal2ConceptArtwork.webp/330px-Primal2ConceptArtwork.webp?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser